Ah Phæbus! ah Mufes! what fustian is here,

I'll have Patience no longer, no longer forbear;

But Print my own Works to consute this damn'd Vice,

My Version's exact, and Expression concise;

My Poem's Heroic, and yet is so large,

It requires some Hundreds the Press to discharge.

Seven Years have I toiled, to make the Piece fine,

And labour'd more hard than a Slave in a Mine;

But now it is Perfect. — I'll bring it Tomorrow,

And read it you all — Thought I to my Sorrow:

To escape this sad Judgment no way cou'd I find,

Had n't Fortune prov'd more than expectedly kind;

